  "notes": "SID Method: momentum-confirmation system trading off RSI extremes. Long entry requires RSI to have touched below 30 within last 10 bars, now rising but still below 50, with MACD line rising for 2 consecutive bars. Short entry requires RSI touched above 70, now falling but still above 50, MACD falling 2 bars. Exit when RSI crosses 50. Weekly RSI direction is a visual gate (assess by eye, not a hard filter — per STRATEGIES.md). LORP: Lorentzian Classification ML trend-following pullback system, long-only daily. Validated entry gate (see STRATEGIES.md / LORP_optimization_log.md / confluence_check.py): an LC Premium Buy fires WITH MACD0 up (MACD >= Signal); the LC Buy is PRIMARY and is not excluded for failing context. Aroon, RVOL and ADX are context only — NOT validated as predictive. Price>EMA50>SMA200 and MACD>0 are upstream TV-Screener pre-filters, not the gate. ETFs average ~4.0 PF vs ~1.5 PF for individual stocks.",
